{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229031-3e-craft-probability-and-cost-calculation","id":1229031,"title":"[3E] Craft Probability and Cost Calculation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-20T17:46:42-07:00","id":1229031,"title":"[3E] Craft Probability and Cost Calculation","content":"I've made an R script (well, two, one for solars and one for terrestrials) to calculate the probability of success and and average cxp cost for superior projects of any given rating by 3E characters with any given build (it can also calculate the completion probability for legendary projects, but not yet the average wxp cost). The script can also give the average numbers of major and minor projects needed per superior project and allows customisation for various other options such as success probability-cost tradeoffs and how brightly you can afford to let your anima flare. The forum is saying that they're invalid files to upload (I guess because they're programs and so could potentially contain viruses), but I'm happy to use them to answer questions for anyone who wants me to, or to provide them to people who want them if I can find a way.<br /> I'd make a table of the outputs from different inputs, but there's too many different inputs (artifact rating, ability rating, number of charms, essence) so I'm not sure what to use for the rows and columns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11290,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","user":"rj.au","date":". 06-20-2018, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T20:05:39-07:00","id":1229054,"title":"","content":"Some results:<br /> Terrestrial:<br /> Imago-Hatching Realization is a must-have for crafting powerful artefacts - it increases the rating of artefact that can typically be successfully made by one (from 3 to 4 at essence 3-4 and from 4 to 5 at essence 5). Ephemeral Form Composition is a must-have for crafting artefacts frequently, letting you craft around one artifact rated essence-1 per major project. Dragonblooded have neglegible chances of successfully completing legendary projects in any circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11290,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","user":"rj.au","date":". 06-20-2018, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T09:43:15-07:00","id":1229168,"title":"","content":"If you're willing to handle questions, here's my build:<br /> 10 dice base (so 20 with excellency)<br /> Can re-roll 10s<br /> Get 10 extra non-charm dice and a non-charm success <br /> <br /> So, basically, 30 dice (10s are of course double, but also give a re-roll), plus 1 success.<br /> <br /> What are average numbers of rolls for me to do each level of artefact?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T14:15:26-07:00","id":1229226,"title":"","content":"2: 2.9<br /> 3: 4.5<br /> 4: 5.7 assuming you complete it - 46% chance you don't<br /> 5: 6 assuming you complete it, 98% chance you don't<br /> NA: less than 0.01% chance of completing it at all.<br /> <br /> If you were wanting the average number of attempts assuming you could roll as many attempts as you wanted, they are<br /> 2: 2.9<br /> 3: 4.5<br /> 4: 6.5<br /> 5: 8.4<br /> NA: 16.3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11290,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","user":"rj.au","date":". 06-21-2018, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T10:42:34-07:00","id":1229397,"title":"","content":"That's actually quite useful, thanks.<br /> I wasn't really going to try any level 5 artefacts, because they take too long (since I can't lower the time to a week like I can with levels 2-4), but one of the other players was interested in me making a level 4 artefact for them, so that's useful to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}